// ────────────── Named Workspaces ──────────────
// https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri/wiki/Configuration:-Named-Workspaces
//
// Four persistent, named workspaces that categorise the desktop. Unlike the
// dynamic workspaces these always exist and take the low indices, so
// Mod+1/2/3/4 reach them by category while Mod+5.. still cover the dynamic ones
// that keep spawning below.
//
//   1 web        — browsers          (zen)
//   2 terminals  — shells            (kitty)
//   3 code       — editors / IDEs    (GoLand, VSCode Insiders)
//   4 extras     — chat & catch-all  (Beeper, everything else)
//
// Index order note: on a fresh niri start these follow declaration order
// (web=1, terminals=2, code=3, extras=4). A live config-reload instead inserts
// each named workspace at the top as it is read, so mid-session they can show
// reversed until the next login. This is cosmetic only — the open-on-workspace
// rules below match by NAME, so app routing is identical either way.
//
// Apps are steered onto these by open-on-workspace rules in cfg/rules.kdl.

workspace "web"
workspace "terminals"
workspace "code"
workspace "extras"
